    "hikouki (plane)"
   ],
   "flags": [],
   "use": "Heard as okureteru (it's running late) or okurete (because it was late), as in gomen, densha okurete... Casual speech drops ga, so densha okureta means the train was late. Swap ga for ni and you are the one who was late: densha ni okureta (I missed the train).",
   "notes": "When the line has stopped altogether: densha tomatteru. A clock running slow is also tokei ga okureteru (fast is susunderu).",
   "example": {
