   "flags": [],
   "use": "Mostly heard as a check or a result: maniau? (will we make it?), maniatta (made it), maniawanai (we won't make it). The noun drops once the train is clear. Once it has gone, say densha ni okureta, or more casually nogashita or noriokureta (I missed it). For the last train people usually say shuuden nakunatta (the last train's gone) or shuuden nogashita.",
   "notes": "maniattemasu also means 'we're fine, no thanks', a common way to turn away a door-to-door or phone salesperson.",
   "example": {
    "romaji": "isoganai to, densha ni maniawanai yo.",
