   "use": "Mostly said beforehand while rushing: densha ni okurechau! (I'll miss my train!), densha ni okurenai you ni (so we don't miss it). Keep the ni: with no particle, densha okureta is heard as the train running late, which is the usual excuse. Once it has gone, natives usually say noriokureta or nogashita: nebou shite densha noriokureta (I overslept and missed my train).",
   "notes": "With a class or meeting the same frame just means late (jugyou ni okureta); a train doesn't wait, so late means missed.",
