   "use": "Said as a warning or an excuse near midnight: shuuden nakunatchau (I'll miss the last train), shuuden nakunatta (the trains have stopped for the night). Casual speech drops ga. shuuden nogashita (I missed the last train) is just as common and makes it your miss.",
   "notes": "shuuden nanji? (when's your last train?) is the usual question as a night out winds down.",
